---
description: Prevent social posts from linking to content that is not live
alwaysApply: true
---

# External Content Publication Gate

- Create drafts only. Never publish, schedule, or send social content without
  explicit user approval after showing the final text, destination, link, and
  attached image.
- A pull request, branch preview, content date, or draft status is not proof
  that an article is published.
- Before presenting a social post as ready, confirm that the article is merged
  into the default branch and deployed to production.
- Verify the final public article URL returns HTTP `200` with an HTML content
  type and displays the intended article, not a homepage or 404 fallback.
- Verify the Open Graph image URL returns HTTP `200` with an image content type.
- Attach the intended social image explicitly when the publishing surface
  supports attachments. Do not depend only on link-preview scraping.
- If any check fails, keep the post as a draft and report the exact blocker.
